# Quick Start Guide - Trade Allocation System

**One-page reference for getting started quickly**

---

## Prerequisites Checklist

```
[ ] .NET 8 SDK installed (dotnet --version shows 8.0.x)
[ ] SQL Server running (localhost or localhost\SQLEXPRESS)
[ ] Git installed
[ ] VS Code or Visual Studio 2022
```

---

## Installation (5 Minutes)

### 1. Install .NET 8 SDK

```bash
# Windows (PowerShell as Admin)
winget install Microsoft.DotNet.SDK.8

# macOS
brew install --cask dotnet-sdk

# Linux (Ubuntu)
wget https://dot.net/v1/dotnet-install.sh
bash dotnet-install.sh --channel 8.0
```

### 2. Verify Installation

```bash
dotnet --version
# Should show: 8.0.x
```

---

## Build the Solution (2 Minutes)

```bash
cd C:\Users\mcsis\TradeAllocationSystem

# Restore packages
dotnet restore

# Build all projects
dotnet build

# Should see: Build succeeded
```

---

## Database Setup (10 Minutes)

### Create Databases

```sql
-- Run in SQL Server Management Studio or Azure Data Studio
CREATE DATABASE TradeAllocationCompliance;
CREATE DATABASE TradeAllocationBooking;
CREATE DATABASE TradeAllocationFund;
CREATE DATABASE TradeAllocationReference;
GO
```

### Update Connection Strings

Edit `appsettings.json` in each API project:

```json
{
  "ConnectionStrings": {
    "DefaultConnection": "Server=localhost;Database=TradeAllocation[ServiceName];Trusted_Connection=True;TrustServerCertificate=True"
  }
}
```

**Note**: Replace `localhost` with `localhost\\SQLEXPRESS` if using SQL Express

